      "writtenOn": "2022-12-01T08:52:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s a good question. Currently this verification is done in init (after pvmfw launches payload, but before the payload actually runs). If the verification fails in init, a reboot is triggered. That\u0027s the behavior or both protected and unprotected VMs. Even when the verification fails, we still destroy the process (line 461).\n\nb/256148034 is supposed to do the verification inside pvmfw, and then reboots[1] when it fails. Here I\u0027m a bit confused, why do we need to duplicate the same check in pvmfw? Anyway this verification will be done in init later.\n\n[1] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Virtualization/pvmfw/src/entry.rs;l\u003d60;drc\u003d277c0f15be43a8eeb4cb5dc1e09a582707b4d792",
      "parentUuid": "fc0cbd92_2c4ff6b4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 429,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 429,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "e6d1ccde9c6286dc7d7112aa65ea2b4263e89e7b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cd3b6f90_c4c4c10d",
        "filename": "tests/hostside/java/com/android/microdroid/test/MicrodroidHostTests.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 429,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-01T10:26:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Here I\u0027m a bit confused, why do we need to duplicate the same check in pvmfw? Anyway this verification will be done in init later.\n\nAs we discussed on Friday, I believe that your confusion comes from an assumption that these checks are validating the same inputs but it\u0027s very unlikely that they are as it wouldn\u0027t make sense to validate the kernel from a userspace process.\n\n\u003e Currently this verification is done in init\n\nCould you share a pointer to that code?\n\n\u003e ... done in init (after pvmfw launches payload, but before the payload actually runs)\n\npvmfw executes the kernel, it doesn\u0027t deal with userspace (init and the payload) beyond validating the ramdisk.",
      "parentUuid": "c7c46f3b_c0a95729",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 429,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 429,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "e6d1ccde9c6286dc7d7112aa65ea2b4263e89e7b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d43b0ff6_c5d836d7",
        "filename": "tests/hostside/java/com/android/microdroid/test/MicrodroidHostTests.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 429,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-01T11:17:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the input! My understanding is that, currently the boot order of the main components and the things they verify are\n\n1/ pvmfw: it is supposed to verify the microdroid_kernel image (public key, vbmeta, partitions) with libavb\n2/ init: verify some slots[3] with libavb[2] (Question: is there an easy way to deploy changes in system/core/init without flashing the whole device?)\n3/ microdroid_manager: verify vbmeta in apexes with libavb, verify apks with apkverify)\n\nA problem for this test is that it resigns all the images[1], so from users\u0027 perspective the boot always fails even when pvmfw does nothing. It\u0027s also hard to tell init fails in *which* image verification. It could be better to resign only the kernel image in this test IMO, and if we want to test init failure, we resign only the image init cares about. We can also get rid of the log-based tests like this, as we only need to check whether Microdroid launches or not instead of parsing the log.\n\n[1] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Virtualization/apex/sign_virt_apex.py;l\u003d16;drc\u003db81e821b3f37e2a67dba1292e1dc2715287d32f4\n[2] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:system/core/init/first_stage_mount.cpp;l\u003d785;drc\u003de321b113d6fb0e618edfbc27b5530806ae274ac8\n[3] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:system/core/fs_mgr/fs_mgr_slotselect.cpp;l\u003d51;drc\u003d81c34f74fac77836f966ea771c6f9763d4cc4aca",
      "parentUuid": "cd3b6f90_c4c4c10d",
      "range": {
